Description:
 edulution-linbo-vdi - VDI service for linuxmuster.net on Proxmox
Changes:
 edulution-linbo-vdi (1.1.9) noble; urgency=medium
 .
   * Windows masters are no longer rebuilt every cycle: machine "q35" now
     matches the versioned type Proxmox pins (pc-q35-*), "pc"/"i440fx"
     matches pc-i440fx-* (closes #31).
   * The primary OS is the first [OS] section with a BaseImage that is not
     StartEnabled = no. Its image decides whether the master is current, its
     Name is the default display name, and it is started (closes #32).
   * The master syncs every OS with an image, then starts the primary one;
     the new group key sync_os limits this to some sections. Master
     descriptions record the size of every synced image, and a change in any
     of them triggers a rebuild (closes #33).
   * The broker hands out only clones whose connect_port (default 3389)
     answers and does not return the same dead VM on a retry. A free clone
     whose connect port stops answering is marked failed after
     livenessTimeout; connect_port 0 restores the old health-port check
     (closes #34).
   * Clones of the current master are started, repaired and replaced while
     a newer master is building; only new clones wait for it (closes #35).
   * Assignments are written with the Proxmox config digest, so two requests
     at the same time cannot get the same clone (closes #36).
   * Before removing a clone the service reads it again and keeps it if it
     was assigned or a user logged in meanwhile; a user with several SMB
     sessions holds all their clones; an interrupted removal is retried
     (closes #37).
   * The broker returns ip, name and hostname of the assigned VM, and a
     missing SPICE ticket no longer fails an RDP request (#38).
   * A VM that cannot be read (e.g. a dropped TLS connection to pveproxy) is
     read again once. If it still fails, the group is skipped for that cycle
     instead of treating the VM as absent, which built a clone and deleted it
     again in the next cycle, or could even start a new master.
